=== Nullable(UInt64): legacy string-wrapped \\N is a null ===
1	1	\N
2	0	42
3	0	43
4	1	\N
5	1	\N
=== Nullable(String): only \\N is a null, the words NULL and null stay strings ===
1	1	\N
2	0	NULL
3	0	null
4	0	hello
5	0	a,b
6	1	\N
=== LowCardinality(Nullable(String)): the same forms ===
1	1	\N
2	0	NULL
3	0	text
=== Nullable(Float64): \\N is a null and NaN still parses ===
1	1	\N
2	0	nan
3	0	1.5
=== Nullable(String) in array mode: the legacy string-wrapped array is unaffected ===
1	['a','b']
2	['c']
